    {
      "form": "single_dose",
      "days": 0,
      "note": "A SINGLE-DOSE container is used in one go: nothing stays in it, so opening it starts no clock — and the box is what the pantry stores, where «apri la scatola» says nothing about the four sealed containers left inside. This rule said 1 day, and a box of 6 glycerol monodose containers (notes: «6 CONTENITORI MONODOSE», 4 pz left, printed date 2028) read «da usare entro 1 gg dall'apertura» — a sealed box declared expired two weeks ago. A form that is really prepared and then kept (a powder to reconstitute) is the exception and belongs in the product's own `med_pao_days`, which the household edits in the medicine sheet.",
      "match": {
        "it": ["fiala", "fiale", "monodose", "flaconcino", "flaconcini", "siringa preriempita"],
        "en": ["vial", "vials", "ampoule", "ampoules", "single dose", "single-dose", "prefilled syringe"],
